y are not"},{"surface":"இவண்","parts":[{"text":"இவண்","lemma":"இவண்","gloss":"here"}],"gloss":"here"},{"surface":"உடற்றி","parts":[{"text":"உடற்றி","lemma":"உடற்றி","gloss":"having provoked"}],"gloss":"having provoked"},{"surface":"யோரே","parts":[{"text":"யோரே","lemma":"யோரே","gloss":"those who"}],"gloss":"those who","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"செறுவர்","parts":[{"text":"செறுவர்","lemma":"செறுவர்","gloss":"enemies"}],"gloss":"enemies"},{"surface":"நோக்கிய","parts":[{"text":"நோக்கிய","lemma":"நோக்கிய","gloss":"that looked at"}],"gloss":"that looked at"},{"surface":"கண்","parts":[{"text":"கண்","lemma":"கண்","gloss":"eye"}],"gloss":"eye"},{"surface":"தன்","parts":[{"text":"தன்","lemma":"தன்","gloss":"his"}],"gloss":"his"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"சிறுவனை","parts":[{"text":"சிறுவன்","lemma":"சிறுவன்","gloss":"little son"},{"text":"ஐ","lemma":"ஐ","gloss":"accusative suffix"}],"gloss":"little son"},{"surface":"நோக்கியுஞ்","parts":[{"text":"நோக்கியும்","lemma":"நோக்கு","gloss":"even having looked at"},{"text":"ஞ்","lemma":"ஞ்","gloss":"sandhi consonant"}],"gloss":"even having looked at"},{"surface":"சிவப்பு","parts":[{"text":"சிவப்பு","lemma":"சிவப்பு","gloss":"redness"}],"gloss":"redness"},{"surface":"ஆனாவே","parts":[{"text":"ஆனா","lemma":"ஆனா","gloss":"does not end"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"does not end"}]}],"literal":"In his hand is the spear, on his feet are the adorned heroic anklets / on his body is sweat, on his throat is a fresh wound / having mixed the great flowers of veṭci and vēṅkai / and worn them beautifully on his curly dark hair / like a strong male elephant that fought a striped tiger / his anger has still not subsided, alas! / They did not survive, those who provoked him here / His eyes that glared at the enemies / even when looking at his own little son, their redness does not fade!","translation":"In his hand is the spear, on his feet are the adorned heroic anklets. His body is covered in sweat, and on his throat is a fresh wound. Having mixed the great flowers of veṭci and vēṅkai, he wears them beautifully on his curly dark hair. Like a strong male elephant that has fought a striped tiger, his anger has still not subsided, alas! Those who provoked him here have not survived. His eyes, which glared at his enemies, still do not lose their redness even when he looks at his own little son!","modern":"அவனுடைய கையில் வேல் இருக்கிறது; கால்களில் அணிந்த வீரக்கழல் இருக்கிறது. உடம்பில் வியர்வை வழிகிறது; கழுத்தில் புதிய காயம் இருக்கிறது. வெட்சி மலர்களையும் பெரிய வேங்கை மலர்களையும் கலந்து, தன் சுருண்ட கரிய தலைமுடியில் அழகாகச் சூடியிருக்கிறான். வரிகளையுடைய புலியோடு போரிட்ட வலிமையான ஆண் யானையைப் போல, அவனுடைய சினம் இன்னும் தணியவில்லை, அந்தோ! அவனிடம் இங்குப் பகைமை பாராட்டியவர்கள் உயிர் பிழைக்கவில்லை. பகைவர்களைக் கோபத்துடன் நோக்கிய அவனுடைய கண்கள், தன் சிறு மகனைப் பார்க்கும்போதும் இன்னும் சிவப்புக் குறையாமல் இருக்கின்றனவே!","explanation":"This poem is composed by the famous poet Avvaiyar in praise of the chieftain Adhiyaman Neduman Anchi, belonging to the Puram theme of Vagai (victory). The poet describes the fierce warrior-king returning from the battlefield, still filled with intense battle-rage. He is adorned with mixed veṭci and vēṅkai flowers on his dark curly hair, and bears a fresh wound on his throat, resembling a victorious war elephant that has just fought a tiger. The poet marvels at how his eyes, which glared red with fury at his enemies, still retain their terrifying redness even when he looks tenderly at his own little son. Key words like 'சினனே' (anger) and 'சிவப்பு ஆனாவே' (redness does not fade) highlight the enduring intensity of his martial spirit.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,1.0],[1.0,1.2],[1.2,1.48],[1.48,1.9],[1.9,2.7],[2.7,3.0],[3.0,3.7],[3.7,4.1],[4.12,4.15],[4.2,5.3],[5.3,5.5],[5.5,6.1],[6.1,6.4],[6.5,7.4],[7.4,7.6],[7.6,7.7],[7.7,8.1],[8.1,8.8],[8.8,9.6],[9.6,9.9],[9.9,9.9],[9.9,10.4],[10.4,11.0],[11.0,11.8],[11.8,12.4],[12.